<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harput Ulu Mosque</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1156–1157</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ulu Cami of Harput</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harput">Harput</a> Ulu Mosque is a mosque in the old town of Harput in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, built in 1156–1157 under the Artuqid ruler Fakhr al-Din Qara Arslan. One of the oldest mosques in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, it is built of brick and stone, and its minaret leans noticeably.</p></div>
